        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Before cars, people rode horses."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "Horses are fast."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "A horse and rider can go 45 kilometers (km) an hour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "But riding horses is difficult in cities."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "It is dangerous, too."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "And horses make a mess."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "In 1885, people made the first gasoline car."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "It went 16 km an hour."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Soon, cars were faster than horses."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "They went 80 km an hour."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "How fast can cars go today?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
